// Product layer -- highest priority of the four gl_screen layout layers.
// Load order: reference -> inch -> screen -> product. Last definition wins.
//
// Syntax (parsed by /etc/gl_screen/scripts/kv_config.lua):
//   KEY 123          integer
//   KEY 1.5          float
//   KEY "text"       string
//   KEY &POINTER     pointer
//   KEY OTHER_KEY    reference to another key
//
// Compiled defaults cannot be read out of the gl_screen binary, so values are
// absolute, not deltas. Find them by writing a key, running
// `/etc/init.d/gl_screen reload`, and looking at the panel.
//
// Every addressable key is listed in analysis/screen_keys.csv.
// Examples, commented out:
//
// HOME_WIFI_CARD_X 24
// HOME_WIFI_CARD_Y 96
// HOME_WIFI_CARD_WIDTH 200
// LOCK_SCREEN_DATA_STYLE1_MINUTE_LABEL_COLOR 0xD98E4F
